#!/usr/bin/env python3
# D2z: surface_patch.side_face_step_height and .side_face_area_law.
#
# Geometry is the D2k side_face_flux / D2x side_face_area case verbatim (see
# ./input): a 4 x 4 x 60 block at 2 mm whose corner column is heated ten times
# harder, so it recedes ~10x faster and a STAIRCASE forms whose risers are the
# faces these keys act on.
#
# The closure pays each riser its TRUE sub-cell height
#     delta = |n + phi_S - phi_T|          BOTH columns' TIME-BASED phases
# and corrects the lateral face conductance by
#     g(delta) = (1 - exp(-delta*a)) / (1 - exp(-a)),   a = dz*v/alpha
# with v = dz/dt_i from the column's own trailing flip interval and
# alpha = kappa/(rho*cp), the thermal DIFFUSIVITY.
#
# Variants (4 ranks):
#   ON     side_face_flux = 1, factor 1.0                     the reference
#   STEP   ON + step_height = 1, area_law = step              delta * dz * dy
#   WET    ON + step_height = 1, area_law = wetted            exact ramp
#   STEPA  STEP + side_face_factor_above = 0.0                (D2x's AEXA lesson)
#   FLAT   STEP on a 1 x 1 x 60 column: no lateral neighbour at all
#
# Checks:
#   (a) DEFAULT-OFF: with neither key set the run is BYTE-IDENTICAL to ON --
#       thermo.dat, the removal log, every Level_0 Cell_D. This is what keeps
#       the d2z1.md5 tree reference valid.
#   (b) THE KEYS REACH THE CODE: STEP and WET register delta_mean,
#       delta_fallback_cols and riser_area_ratio; ON registers none of them.
#   (c) THE TWO LAWS DIFFER, AND IN THE RIGHT DIRECTION. wetted charges the
#       EXACT ramp sqrt(1+d^2)-1, which is below d for every d > 0, so WET must
#       draw strictly less side power than STEP. ⚠ NOT delta^2/2: that is the
#       small-step limit and it OVERcharges at d >= 2 (2.0 against a true
#       1.236), which is exactly where A's cascaded floor lives.
#   (d) EACH LAW HAS THE SIGN IT MUST. riser_area_ratio is assigned-area over
#       the OTHER law's, so step's is > 1 and wetted's is < 1 for every delta.
#       ⚠ NOT compared row-by-row BETWEEN the runs: STEP and WET deposit
#       different heat, so their geometries diverge and their delta populations
#       are not the same. Reciprocity is a per-face identity at equal delta and
#       is checked in closed form (d2), together with the numbers that separate
#       the exact ramp from the withdrawn delta^2/2 limit (d3).
#   (e) g(1) = 1 EXACTLY, so an unlagged full-cell step is untouched. Checked
#       directly on the closed form rather than through a run.
#   (f) THE LEDGER TWIN MIRRORS. max|ledger_err| <= 1e-12 relative AND the
#       ABSOLUTE residual err*|E_src| <= 1e-9 J. ledger_err is relative to
#       E_src, so gating area off shrinks it and a relative bar alone is the
#       wrong instrument (the D2x lesson). A genuine mirror failure -- the
#       kernel depositing area the ledger does not count -- would drift by
#       order the uncounted power times time, tens of joules.
#   (g) NOT DILUTED BY ABOVE-PLANE FACES: on STEPA some columns sit above the
#       descending nozzle plane, where side_face_factor_above = 0.0 governs by
#       a DIFFERENT law. delta_mean must still be a below-plane-only mean and
#       side_P_face_above must be exactly 0. D2x's side_w_mean read 0.147
#       because 79 % of late-run faces were above-plane and counted at weight 0.
#   (h) FLAT PLATE: a single column has no lateral neighbour, so there are no
#       risers, side_P_face is 0 and delta_mean is 0. The closure must not
#       invent area where there is no step.
#   (i) THE PARSER REFUSES every mutual exclusion and every orphaned key.
#
# Usage: test            (runs ALAMO, then checks)
#        test <outdir>   (checks existing outputs under <outdir>)

